From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: do not fail AddSensor when the MDNS profile write fails

The HAL's AddSensor sequence programs the MDNS buffer, then asks the
driver to apply the stock motion profile.  The recovered profile write
can fail with -EINVAL; returning that made IMP_ISP_AddSensor fail even
though the buffer was programmed and the main video path is independent
of MDNS.

Log the failure and let the buffer SET succeed so streaming can come up.
---
--- a/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_recovered.c
+++ b/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_recovered.c
@@ -36935,7 +36935,9 @@
             if (mdns) {
                 ret = t41_apply_stock_mdns_profile();
                 if (ret)
-                    return ret;
+                    printk(KERN_WARNING
+                           "t41: MDNS profile apply failed: %d (continuing)\n",
+                           ret);
             }
         }
     } else if (get) {
